<title>ROMANIA: Bucharest bourse gets 52nd listing.</title>
<headline>Bucharest bourse gets 52nd listing.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bucharest bourse said on Wednesday the number of its listings would rise to 52 on Thursday, when one more company would join in trading on the first tier.</p>
<p>The newcomer is the Otel Inox steel mill in Tirgoviste, west of Bucharest, a stock exchange statement said.</p>
<p>Following are details of Otel Inox:</p>
<p>* Share capital: 140.9 billion lei.</p>
<p>* Number of shares: 5,639,985; each share has a face value of 25,000 lei.</p>
<p>* Ownership structure: The State Ownership Fund has a 71.903 percent, Broadhurst Investment Ltd (Cyprus) has 12.524 percent and other holders 15.323 percent.</p>
<p>* Net profit in 1996: 6.87 billion lei; in 1995: 4.53 billion lei.</p>
<p>The Bucharest stock exchange trades eight companies on the first tier.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
